          "tz": 0
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Yonatan Nachum",
          "email": "ynachum@amazon.com",
          "date": "2026-07-22 12:39:20.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20497 efalnd: Add protection against stale Rx completions",
        "message": "LU-20497 efalnd: Add protection against stale Rx completions\n\nOn Rx completion, we immediately fetch the Rx using the pointer stored\nin the WR ID. If the Rx is stale due to NI destroy and creation, we\ndefer an Rx not relevant for the completion resulting in failures in\nunpack flow or even crashes if the Rx is currently not posted so its\nrx_nob is -1. To handle this situation, instead of storing the Rx\naddress in the WR ID, store its index in the first 4 bytes and part of\nthe NI epoch in the upper 4 bytes. This way we can validate the Rx\ncompletion is for the current NI and if not drop it.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nChange-Id: I4c2c60f558fc5130cfc58d1bd7e4bb5dabec868e\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
